# Third-party notices

fil is free software, licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your option)
any later version (GPL-3.0-or-later); the text is in `LICENSE`. The fil binaries also contain the
work of others, under the licenses below. Every one of them is compatible with the GPL-3.0.

This file is generated by `just notices-update` from `about.hbs` and `about.toml` with cargo-about,
for the dependency graph of the release binary: the `fil` package with its default features, its
normal and build dependencies, on the four release targets (x86_64 and aarch64 Linux with musl,
x86_64 and aarch64 macOS). It lists more than any one binary contains: build scripts and
procedural macros run while fil is built, and a crate that one target alone uses is only in that
target's binary. Do not edit it by hand.

The source code of a release, with every dependency below, is in its source archive,
`fil-<version>-source.tar.gz`, published with the binaries.

