The standard library includes the work of others. The crates it is built from and the Unicode
data in `core` (Unicode-3.0) are listed, each with its notice, in `COPYRIGHT-library.html`, which
each Rust release ships (in `share/doc/rust/` of the toolchain).

The binaries also contain LLVM runtime code that the toolchain links in: parts of compiler-rt (in
`compiler_builtins`) and, in the Linux binaries, LLVM's libunwind and the `crtbegin.o` and
`crtend.o` objects. That code is under the Apache License 2.0 with the LLVM exception
(Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception), which lets portions embedded in an object form, as here, be
redistributed without meeting sections 4(a), 4(b) and 4(d) of the license, so it needs no notice
in a binary. The Rust project lists it under `src/llvm-project` in `COPYRIGHT.html`, which it
ships beside `COPYRIGHT-library.html`.

